-- #1292 (S0), THIRD SEAM: `eval.evalModulesRootEnvWith` -- the driver the
-- `test "…"` phase, the prop runner and the repl actually use (test_cmd.mdk);
-- `evalModulesWith` serves doctests only.  A fix wired into the other two module
-- drivers alone would look correct under every check that never runs `medaka test`.
--
-- Also pins the `Pass`/`Fail` EXEMPTION.  `verdict.mdk` declares constructors
-- spelled `Pass`/`Fail`, colliding with stdlib `test.mdk`'s `Expectation` -- and
-- `tools/test_runner.mdk` reads a test body's result as a BARE `VCon "Pass"` /
-- `VCon "Fail"` by spelling.  Renaming those would send every test in this file
-- down `runOneTest`'s `other => Errored` arm, so all three below would report
-- `ERROR` rather than `ok`.
--
-- 🚨 EXPECTED REPORT HAND-DERIVED, held INLINE in test/diff_compiler_test.sh (no
-- capturable golden), because the buggy base would have enshrined the wrong answer:
--   * `mkA 7` is built inside amodl, so it is amodl's `Box` : TA -> "amod"
--   * `Box 5` is bmodl's `Box` (the only `Box` this file imports) : TB -> "bmod"
--   * `verdictLabel (Fail "x")` is verdict.mdk's own `Fail` -> "fail:x"
-- ⚠️ The `ok` lines carry LINE NUMBERS: keep edits above line-count-neutral.
import test.{expectEqual}
import labeliface.{Label, label}
import amodl.{TA, mkA}
import bmodl.{TB, Box}
import verdict.{Verdict(..), verdictLabel}

test "amod's own Box tags TA" = expectEqual (label (mkA 7)) "amod"

test "the imported bmod Box tags TB" = expectEqual (label (Box 5)) "bmod"

test "a Pass/Fail collision does not break the test runner" = expectEqual (verdictLabel (Fail "x")) "fail:x"
